Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||09-19-2001||10:42 AM||||This place makes pullies down to the 3" AND an intercooler that still fits under the hood (barely).  The guy at Dells with the Aldino was running the 3" pulley and intercooler- nice.  Why recreate the wheel?<P><A HREF="http://www.thrasher-ep.com/L67_htm/pulley.shtm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thrasher-ep.com/L67_htm/pulley.shtm</A><P><BR>BTW: the concept is REALLY cool (no pun intended)  Maybe combining the SC cooler & an Intercooler...?<BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 09-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||09-19-2001||10:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR>[B]"""Another benefit is increased resistance to detonation because of the lower charge air temp.  In fact, the air charge is now so cool that you can run a 2.3 ratio blower pulley on regular premium fuel without detonation""<P>What diameter is a 2.3 ratio pulley??? This is from thrashers page about their intercooler setup.<BR>B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>A 2.3 ratio pulley is 3"<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||09-19-2001||11:48 AM||||MintGreen:<P>My thoughts exactly , why reinvent the wheel. Thrasher is well known , and whenI was at the pontiac nationals I watched a GTP run mid 12's with no NOS ..<P>gotta respect that. Then the guy drove it home!<P>JM ||||reg||1
