Z||000014||lildevil||09-19-2001||08:27 PM||||I think Pontiac is doing us 3800Fiero owners a service by keeping us informed on the new products being developed this coming year. And from what i understand there will be ALOT this winter. Howzabout a PCM that gives 40 HP?  Anyways...I am holding off all my mods til next Spring to give every one time to get there products out to market.  And tested thoroughly i hope.  Suddenly the 12's don't look so far away.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000015||pontiacs4me||09-20-2001||02:20 AM||||the L67 is such an awesome engine to mod. years of development in the 3800 have given us an awesome platform to build some wild stuff.  this is only the beginning.   we have so many ideas.<P>about the 40 hp pcm, I met the guy who has the only one in existance.  I dont know if it is some sort of hoax or what, from what ive heard is that thrasher developed the pcm, and someone stole the code.  So now they are back to the drawing board trying to write a code into the pcm that makes it impossible to replicate.  Hopefully it will hit the market by spring.  Hopefully in time for the fiero shootout.  I should have my L67 swap complete by mid January.||||reg||1
